AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03411222> "\"Most fish are ectothermic ('cold-blooded'), allowing their body temperatures to vary as ambient temperatures change, though some of the large active swimmers like white shark and tuna can hold a higher core temperature.\" - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish"@en)
